Package: sbyoracle
Title: Oracle Database Routines and Tagged SQL Diagnostic Reports
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Joao B. G.", "de Brito", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "177784222+JoaoSabby@users.noreply.github.com")
Description: Provides a growing collection of R routines for Oracle Database
    19c and later. Generates comprehensive diagnostic reports for tagged SQL
    statements using an explicit DBI connection, including cursor metadata,
    execution plans, resource statistics, optimizer settings, captured bind
    variables, and adaptive cursor sharing information. Real-Time SQL
    Monitoring is disabled by default and can be explicitly enabled.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports:
    DBI,
    glue,
    stringr
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    ROracle
Config/testthat/edition: 3
URL: https://github.com/JoaoSabby/sbyoracle
BugReports: https://github.com/JoaoSabby/sbyoracle/issues
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.0.0
